@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] siwc-uses-its-official-registration-contract
The user-operated SIWC flow MUST use the documented OpenAI public-client registration,
stable host ID, system browser and exact 127.0.0.1 HTTP loopback callback. Every attempt
MUST have fresh state, nonce and S256 PKCE. First registration MUST exchange with the
issued callback client ID, never dynamic_agent_client; returning authorization MUST
retain its selected issued client and verified subject. Hosted approval MUST NOT be
inferred from OSS source or an identity-only token. Source: Tavi's 22 Oct provider
instruction and official OpenAI SIWC registration/sign-in documentation checked that day.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] siwc-identity-and-plan-permission-are-verified
ID tokens MUST verify an allowed asymmetric signature against the fixed issuer's JWKS,
exact issuer, issued client audience, expiry, issued-at time and original nonce before
identity is trusted. The immutable issuer/client/subject tuple MUST own the registration;
email MUST NOT merge registrations. Inference MUST require the actually granted direct
ChatGPT plan permission and captured current connection; identity-only consent MUST NOT
advertise plan usage. Source: official SIWC registration and accounts/session docs,
and Tavi's 21 Oct account/provider isolation requirement.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] siwc-tokens-stay-in-protected-custody
Access, refresh and retained ID tokens MUST stay in owner/registration-bound encrypted
custody and MUST NOT enter native bodies, browser storage, logs, Debug or arbitrary
requests. OAuth/JWKS requests MUST refuse redirects/proxies and have finite time/body
limits and safe errors. Refresh MUST serialize for its registration and atomically
store the rotating replacement without resurrecting a retired source. Disconnect MUST
retire local use before remote revocation, and distinguish unconfirmed remote revocation.
Source: Tavi's 22 Oct custody boundary and official SIWC accounts/session documentation.
